From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Tiziano=20M=C3=BCller?= <tiziano.mueller@hpe.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Mar 2026 14:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] kbuild: fix parallel build race in cxi tests
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

tests/cxi/single_client and tests/cxi/multi_client both list
../common/test_common.o in their module component objects. With parallel
builds (-jN), kbuild descends into both directories simultaneously and
both attempt to compile common/test_common.o, racing on the .d
dependency file:

  fixdep: error opening file: .../common/.test_common.o.d:
    No such file or directory

The existing .NOTPARALLEL with target arguments does not work in the
kbuild context: the subdirectory entries are data for kbuild's own
scripts/Makefile.build descent mechanism, not make rules that
target-specific .NOTPARALLEL (GNU make 4.4+) can serialize.

Replace with bare .NOTPARALLEL to serialize subdirectory descent at this
level. Since this Makefile contains only obj-y subdirectory entries (no
local objects), the sole effect is ordering the descent -- compilation
within each subdirectory remains fully parallel.

Signed-off-by: Tiziano Mueller <tiziano.mueller@hpe.com>
---
 Makefile | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Makefile b/Makefile
index 1234567..abcdefg 100644
--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -54,7 +54,12 @@ rpm: $(PACKAGE)-$(VERSION).tar.gz
 
 else
 
-.NOTPARALLEL: tests/cxi/single_client/ tests/cxi/multi_client/
+# Serialize kbuild subdirectory descent. tests/cxi/single_client/ and
+# tests/cxi/multi_client/ both compile ../common/test_common.o, causing a
+# parallel build race on the .d dependency file. Target-specific .NOTPARALLEL
+# does not work here as obj-y entries are kbuild data, not make rules.
+# Bare .NOTPARALLEL serializes descent order only; per-subdir builds stay parallel.
+.NOTPARALLEL:
 
 obj-y += kfi/
 obj-y += prov/cxi/
